 R←Test_Select_017(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;⎕IO;⎕ML;r
⍝ Exercise "SelectHelp", the help `Select` puts on display when the user enters a "?".
⍝ Needs neither a user nor automation.
⍝ The help was introduced in 3.1.0
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1
 R←T._Failed

 ⍝ Every line is indented by two spaces and introduced by an asterisk:
 r←C.SelectHelp 0 1 1 5
 →T.PassesIf∧/'  * '∘≡¨4↑¨r

 ⍝ Multiple items, all keywords on offer, and the user may select nothing:
 →T.PassesIf 6=≢r
 →T.PassesIf∨/∊'3-6'∘⍷¨r
 →T.PassesIf∨/∊'a~3 5'∘⍷¨r
 →T.PassesIf∨/∊'a~3-5'∘⍷¨r
 →T.PassesIf∨/∊'quit'∘⍷¨r
 →T.PassesIf∨/∊'<enter>'∘⍷¨r

 ⍝ A single item, no keywords at all, and a selection is compulsory:
 r←C.SelectHelp 1 0 0 1
 →T.PassesIf 1=≢r
 →T.PassesIf~∨/∊'3-6'∘⍷¨r
 →T.PassesIf~∨/∊'a~3 5'∘⍷¨r
 →T.PassesIf~∨/∊'quit'∘⍷¨r
 →T.PassesIf~∨/∊'<enter>'∘⍷¨r

 ⍝ "q" is mentioned when quitting is allowed, no matter what else is:
 →T.PassesIf∨/∊'quit'∘⍷¨C.SelectHelp 1 1 0 1
 →T.PassesIf~∨/∊'quit'∘⍷¨C.SelectHelp 0 0 1 9

 ⍝ Ranges are mentioned as soon as more than one item may be selected:
 →T.PassesIf∨/∊'3-6'∘⍷¨C.SelectHelp 1 0 0 2
 →T.PassesIf~∨/∊'3-6'∘⍷¨C.SelectHelp 1 0 0 1

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
